The current solution's swap neighborhood only considers swaps involving the single worst GPU. Extending swaps to all GPU pairs (like Program 4 did, but without the slower iterated local search) should find slightly better maxima while keeping execution fast. I'll also add a simple plateau move (accept equal-max moves off the worst GPU) as a light escape mechanism.

Two changes:

**Change 1:** Extend the swap phase to try swaps between any GPU pair, not just those involving the worst GPU.

**Change 2:** Add a plateau-escape step: if no improving move/swap exists, try a move off the worst GPU that keeps the max unchanged (strictly reduces second-worst pressure), accepted at most a few times.

