- Full pairwise swaps catch improving swaps that don't involve the current worst GPU (e.g., between the 2nd and 3rd worst GPUs), which the previous version missed. This was the key strength of Program 4's refinement.
- The plateau move lets the search leave flat local optima by shifting load off the worst GPU when the max stays the same, potentially unlocking further improving moves — a lightweight version of Program 4's perturbation, without its runtime cost.
- Execution time should remain well under the limit (Program 4's full pairwise swaps ran in 0.19s; this version skips the random restarts, so it should be closer to ~0.05s), keeping the combined score's time component low.
